# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. .env is git-ignored —
# never commit real Client Secrets (see apps/api/oauth.go challenge #5).

# Google OAuth app (console.cloud.google.com > APIs & Services > Credentials)
# Authorized redirect URI: {API_PUBLIC_URL}/api/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# GitHub OAuth app (github.com/settings/developers > OAuth Apps)
# Authorization callback URL: {API_PUBLIC_URL}/api/auth/github/callback
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Where the API itself is reachable from the browser during the OAuth
# redirect round-trip. Defaults to http://localhost:8080 if unset.
API_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Where to send the browser after a successful OAuth login, AND the only
# origin the API accepts cross-origin requests from (see allowedOrigin() in
# apps/api/main.go) — in production this must be the real frontend origin,
# e.g. https://whiparc.com, not left unset. Defaults to http://localhost:3000
# (and "*" for CORS) if unset, which is only appropriate for local dev.
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Transactional Email Delivery (Optional) ---
# Leave unset in local development: verification links will print directly
# to the API console logs. For production delivery, configure Resend or SMTP.
#
# Option A: Resend (Recommended for SaaS)
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_123456789
# EMAIL_FROM=Whiparc <noreply@whiparc.com>
#
# Option B: Standard SMTP
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.mailgun.org
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=postmaster@yourdomain.com
# SMTP_PASS=your-smtp-password
# EMAIL_FROM=Whiparc <noreply@whiparc.com>
#
# Option C: Strict DNS MX validation on signup
# STRICT_EMAIL_VALIDATION=true

# --- Billing (Paddle) — product-memory 08.5 item G1 ---
# Leave unset in local development: billing endpoints return clear "not
# configured" errors instead of silently failing. Paddle is the
# merchant-of-record integrator for now (see apps/api/billing.go's
# BillingProvider doc comment) — "sandbox" below is Paddle's own free test
# environment, not this app's DB_DRIVER choice.
#
# "sandbox" (default if unset) or "production" — selects which Paddle API
# host apps/api/billing.go talks to.
PADDLE_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
# Server-side API key (Paddle > Developer tools > Authentication). Used for
# customer-portal sessions and subscription seat updates — never sent to the
# browser.
PADDLE_API_KEY=
# Secret for the notification destination pointed at
# {API_PUBLIC_URL}/api/billing/webhook (Paddle > Developer tools >
# Notifications > your destination). Sandbox and production destinations
# each have their own secret — never share one between them.
PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# The Pro plan's recurring per-seat price id (looks like pri_01h...), from
# Paddle > Catalog > Prices. Sandbox and production prices have different
# ids — this must match PADDLE_ENVIRONMENT above.
PADDLE_PRICE_ID_PRO=
# Plan limits (Free: 3 members, 3 active projects, no custom nodes, no Pro
# templates). Unset = enforced exactly when PADDLE_API_KEY is set, so a
# self-hosted install with no billing stays uncapped. "true"/"false" forces it.
# PLAN_ENFORCEMENT=
# Client-side token (Paddle > Developer tools > Authentication), safe to
# expose to the browser — read by the Next.js app (apps/web) to open Paddle
# Checkout. This repo has no apps/web/.env.example (its vars are supplied by
# the hosting platform, e.g. Vercel project settings) — these two are listed
# here only so both halves of the Paddle config are documented in one place.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_ENV=sandbox

# --- Production-only secrets (leave unset for local dev; each has a
# dev-only fallback that logs a warning and must never be used publicly) ---

# Encrypts every stored cloud credential (apps/api/vault). Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
WHIPARC_MASTER_KEY=

# Signs every session token this API issues. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
JWT_SECRET=

# Shared secret authenticating the agent-gateway <-> api internal calls; must
# match on both services (see docker-compose.hosted.yml). Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
GATEWAY_RUNNER_SECRET=

# Selects the SQL backend for `go run .` and plain docker-compose.yml.
# Unset (or "sqlite") keeps the default local SQLite file; set to "postgres"
# for a hosted-style deployment, with DATABASE_URL pointing at the Postgres
# instance (e.g. a Supabase connection string). docker-compose.hosted.yml
# does NOT read DB_DRIVER from here — it always runs on Postgres, via its
# own bundled `postgres` service by default. DATABASE_URL here still
# overrides that stack's target if you want it to point somewhere else
# (a real scratch Supabase project, say) instead of the bundled container.
DB_DRIVER=
DATABASE_URL=

# Which published image tags the docker-compose files pull by default. Both
# default to "stable" (the most recently tagged vX.Y.Z release — see
# publish-api-image.yml / publish-base-image.yml and whiparc/cloud's
# publish-agent-gateway.yml). Override to "dev" or "main" to track a branch
# instead of a tagged release. There is no equivalent tag for the sandbox-ssh
# image (the "local machine" SSH containers) — that one is always built
# locally from source, since it bakes in a per-installation SSH key
# (sandbox/id_rsa.pub, see docs/DEVELOPMENT.md) that a shared published image
# could never match.
API_IMAGE_TAG=
AGENT_GATEWAY_IMAGE_TAG=
